      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The original test checks two class-level modifiers in a single method. I'll improve understandability by splitting assertions into focused test methods, extracting the repeated `getModifiers()` call into a local variable, and using clear method names.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version splits the original single test method into two focused tests (`testCharRangeClassIsNotPublic` and `testCharRangeClassIsFinal`), extracts the repeated `CharRange.class.getModifiers()` call into a local variable in each method, and adds brief Javadoc comments explaining the *why* behind each assertion — all without changing the methods called or the expected outcomes."
